Package: dadaS
Type: Package
Title: DadaS: a faster, more robust fork of DADA2 for amplicon sequence variant inference
Description: DadaS is a fork of DADA2 1.36.0 that gives identical results with default options while
    running faster (alignment, k-mer and p-value kernels, NEON SIMD on ARM), with reproducible
    taxonomy bootstraps, thread-safe error handling, and an optional indel error model (INDEL_RATE).
    From the original description: the dada2 package infers exact amplicon sequence variants (ASVs) from 
    high-throughput amplicon sequencing data, replacing the coarser and less accurate
    OTU clustering approach. The dada2 pipeline takes as input demultiplexed fastq 
    files, and outputs the sequence variants and their sample-wise abundances after 
    removing substitution and chimera errors. Taxonomic classification is available
    via a native implementation of the RDP naive Bayesian classifier, and species-level
    assignment to 16S rRNA gene fragments by exact matching.
